            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>There is disclosed a turbine assembly for a turbocharger. The turbine assembly comprises a housing. The housing comprises first and second volutes, a wall member and a first aperture. The housing defines a flow path between an inlet and an outlet. The housing extends around an axis. The first and second volutes define a respective first and second flow passage. A circumferential outlet portion of each of the first and second volutes is defined by first and second tongues. Each of the first and second tongues comprises a tip. A vane assembly is received in the first aperture. The vane assembly defines a turbine wheel-receiving bore. The vane assembly comprises a plurality of vanes circumferentially distributed about the turbine wheel-receiving bore, each of the plurality of vanes comprising a leading edge and a trailing edge. The wall member and vane assembly define an annular passage between the circumferential outlet portions and the turbine wheel-receiving bore. At least one of the vane assembly and the wall member is axially displaceable relative to the other to adjust the extent to which the annular passage is open.</p>
            </abstract>
